# types.ts

- Extend `UseRenderComponentProps<"tag">` when using `useRender`.
- Custom props listed in the same order used in the component and `mergeProps`: `ref`, `render`, custom, native, `disabled`, `className`, `children`, then rest. See `component-tsx.mdc` for `mergeProps` bag order / locks.
- **Interface** only when adding members. If props are just the host tag props, use `export type XProps = UseRenderComponentProps<"tag">` (empty `interface extends` is lint-illegal).
- Types are the source of truth; `index.ts` re-exports them as `ButtonProps` / `DisclosureRootProps`. Consumers may also use `ComponentProps<typeof …>`.
- One export: inline. Multiple: declare then `EXPORTS` section (`export type { … }`).
